        <div class="fc-delta-reason">No material movement — weekly cadence; next review Sunday. NOTE for Sunday review: The Knesset passed a preliminary (first) reading of a COALITION-SPONSORED dissolution bill 110-0 on May 20 (Al Jazeera, Times of Israel, Haaretz). This is a coalition-managed process designed to control election timing, not a loss of majority. The coalition retains 61+ seats. The bill delegates election date-setting to the House Committee after final (third) reading enactment. Netanyahu targets October 2026; Haredi parties push September 2026. Smotrich remains inside the coalition with no formal departure announced. Full evaluation deferred to Sunday per Codex DA #12.</div>
